1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Welcome to Title22, a focused compliance
workspace for California residential care
facilities for the elderly and community-based
residential care facilities.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Title22 is designed to help a facility stay
inspection ready every day, not only when DSS
is expected. The public experience starts with
a clear promise.

3
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Keep staff credentials current, document
required training, and know exactly what needs
attention.

4
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
The compliance checklist comes preloaded with
Title 22 requirements and the related
regulation references.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:46.000
As work is completed, the readiness score
changes in real time, giving administrators a
quick view of where the facility stands.

6
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.000
Instead of showing only a warning count,
Title22 identifies the item, the responsible
staff member, and the relevant date.

7
00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:08.000
Expiration alerts can surface 90, 30, and 7
days before CPR, first aid, tuberculosis
clearances, live scan, or administrator
certifications expire.

8
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Training records are organized around the
initial 40-hour requirement and continuing
education.

9
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Staff certification tracking keeps essential
clearances together, while role-based access
lets each team member see only what they need.

10
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:29.000
A read-only view can also support an inspection
without opening the entire workspace.

11
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:36.000
The AI compliance assistant is grounded in the
facility's own non-clinical compliance records.

12
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Administrators can ask practical questions,
receive a daily briefing, or use scan-to-fill
to read dates from a CPR card or tuberculosis
clearance.

13
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Confidence indicators make it clear which
extracted fields deserve review.

14
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Title22 also supports structured incident
documentation and an append-only audit log
recording who did what and when.

15
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Entries cannot be quietly edited or deleted,
and the record can be exported for a surveyor.

16
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Privacy is a deliberate boundary.

17
00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Title22 is designed to stay clear of resident
health records, medication administration
records, or clinical decision-making.

18
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:20.000
It rejects sensitive identifiers in incident
entries and never suggests, adjusts, or
comments on medication dosage.

19
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:27.000
No protected health information is required,
and no business associate agreement is needed
for this intended use.

20
00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:47.700
In short, Title22 brings checklists, readiness,
training, certifications, alerts, and
accountable records into one practical
workflow, so compliance work is visible before
inspection day.
